      "comment": "SUNBLISS (5) can bounce back off a let-up. She was last seen contesting the G3 Scarborough Stakes at Caulfield in a race that was dominated on speed by some nice fillies. She'd looked promising before that and this is much easier, especially with two key scratchings. SOUND BYTE (7) has been good in two runs back, beating Nishioka first up at Kilmore who has been competitive in stakes races since, then close up at Bendigo in a solid race. She'll give a sight. FONTEIN JEWEL (1) resumes having contested a Listed race at Flemington before a break. Big weight and 3kg claim here suggest he'll be better for the run but he can figure. HOME TOMURRA (3) next best in the quintet.",
